# Workspace graph state (zonoid/.graph/**) is daemon-written, append-only JSONL. On merge, keep
# our side rather than raising conflicts in machine-generated files that no human resolves.
#
# Requires, once per clone:  git config merge.ours.driver true
# Git has no built-in "ours" low-level merge driver (only text/binary/union), so without that
# config this attribute silently degrades to a normal text merge and still conflicts.
#
# Note: this does NOT cover the root `.graph` submodule. Git resolves submodule gitlinks
# internally and never dispatches them to a custom merge driver, so a gitlink conflict there must
# be resolved by picking a graph commit (see CONTRIBUTING.md, ".graph repository and checkpoints").
**/.graph/** merge=ours
